<title>USA: TABLE - Federal Data Corp sells 144a notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Federal Data Corp sells 144a notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a debt issue from Federal Data Corp was priced Monday via lead manager BT Securities Corp, according to a market source.</p>
<p>BORROWER FEDERAL DATA CORP</p>
<p>AMT $105 MLN	 COUPON 10.125 PCT MATURITY 8/1/2005</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NOTES ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 2/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B3    YIELD 10.125 PCT  PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-MINUS   SPREAD +390 BPS   CALLABLE  NON-CALL FOUR</p>
<p>NOTE: The notes have a 35 percent equity call for 110.125 of the issue.</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
